# But what about Letta memory?

This is why I would **not** simply call Mimo directly everywhere.

The fast session still belongs to:

```text
researcher-v1
```

and therefore still starts from that persistent Letta agent and its memory/state.

You retain:

```text
agent identity
persona
durable memory
MemFS
skills
conversation lineage
agent versioning
```

but remove the expensive computer-use feedback loop from the WorkOrder.

The important insight is:

> **Memory does not require an autonomous tool loop.**

Moltwork needs Letta's persistence much more than it needs Letta Code to decide whether to call `Read` three times.

