# There is an even stronger Moltwork architecture here

The worker shouldn't dynamically discover basic task context through expensive LLM calls either.

Before the model runs:

```text
WorkOrder
   │
   ├── LabBrief from Hydra
   ├── relevant Letta memories
   ├── ProcessVersion
   ├── SkillVersion
   ├── repository map
   ├── git diff
   ├── selected source files
   └── acceptance criteria
          │
          ▼
      ContextPack
          │
          ▼
       ONE CALL
```

In other words, **Moltwork does retrieval; the worker does cognition.**

For example:

```yaml
context_pack:
  task:
    objective: fix failing receipt test

  experience:
    lab_brief: ...
    similar_runs:
      - run_193
      - run_217

  repo:
    changed_files:
      - sdk.py
      - core/receipts.py

    relevant_files:
      - tests/test_receipt_v2.py
      - core/receipts.py

  constraints:
    max_files_changed: 4
    tests:
      - tests/test_receipt_v2.py
```

The model doesn't need:

```text
think
LS
think
Glob
think
Read
think
Grep
think
Read
think
Edit
think
test
think
```

just to discover facts Moltwork can cheaply supply upfront.

That is a huge architecture improvement.

