# Mode 2 — BOUNDED for actual iterative jobs

Some jobs genuinely need feedback.

Example:

```text
generate implementation
         ↓
      run tests
         ↓
tests fail
         ↓
generate repair
```

Don't hand this to an unlimited Letta loop.

Moltwork owns the loop:

```text
CALL 1
Letta Fast Worker
→ patch A

DETERMINISTIC
git apply
pytest
→ failure report

CALL 2
Letta Fast Worker
input:
  original task
  patch A
  exact test failure
→ patch B

DETERMINISTIC
apply
pytest

optional CALL 3
review/final repair
```

That gives you:

```text
max_model_calls = 3
```

as a **hard economic primitive**.

And each invocation can still use the same persistent Letta worker.

This is much better than asking Letta Code to self-determine whether it is finished.

