# Mode 3 — full Letta Agent mode

Keep the current execution mode, but only when it actually earns its cost.

Examples:

```text
open-ended repo investigation
web research where next query depends on result
complex debugging with unknown environment
long-running autonomous hackathon implementation
novel tasks where we don't know the required process yet
```

Then:

```yaml
execution:
  mode: agentic
  max_wall_seconds: 300
  max_cost_usd: 0.25
```

Use `session.abort()` when Moltwork's external budget/time watchdog trips; the current Agent SDK explicitly supports aborting an active turn. ([GitHub][3])

So the economic decision becomes interesting:

```text
TaskFamily × WorkerVersion
          ↓
Hydra history
          ↓
Which execution mode works best?
```

Eventually Hydra learns:

```text
classification.*
FAST wins

hackathon.ideation
FAST wins

code.small_patch
BOUNDED-2 wins

code.unknown_debug
AGENTIC wins

research.web.deep
AGENTIC wins
```

That's actually a more valuable Moltwork capability than simply wrapping Letta.

