# Your current performance note contains two conclusions I would fix

You wrote:

> 16 reasoning + 7 assistant + 1 tool = 24 calls.

Not established.

Those are SDK stream events. In fact, Letta has an open documentation issue specifically because reasoning/assistant `content` in the SDK stream is emitted as append-only deltas. ([GitHub][1])

You also wrote:

> No compounding intelligence within a run (separate calls don't share context).

That's the opposite of the Letta agent loop.

Each successive agent step receives prior reasoning/tool results in context; that's why tool-result continuations exist and why their cost can grow. Letta's loop explicitly rebuilds context before subsequent LLM requests. ([GitHub][6])

So change the performance document to:

```text
Cost:
- N agent steps per WorkOrder
- each step = one LLM invocation
- later steps include accumulated context/tool results
- therefore cost/latency can grow substantially with step count

Streaming events != model invocations.
Measure actual step count/provider requests.
```

